498
00:30:21,000 --> 00:30:23,000
First, what is AP?

499
00:30:23,000 --> 00:30:29,000
So AP classes are university or college level classes that students are taking while they're

500
00:30:29,000 --> 00:30:31,000
still in high school.

501
00:30:31,000 --> 00:30:35,000
But there is a standardized exam that they can take as well in May.

502
00:30:35,000 --> 00:30:39,000
And if they do well enough on that exam, they actually get university or college credit

503
00:30:39,000 --> 00:30:42,000
for that course as well.

504
00:30:42,000 --> 00:30:47,000
Yeah, so let's get into why you'd want to take an AP class.

505
00:30:47,000 --> 00:30:51,000
Lots of reasons, but I think the most important is you're developing really strong university

506
00:30:51,000 --> 00:30:55,000
level skills to get you ready for that next level of learning.

507
00:30:55,000 --> 00:31:00,000
We all know that the transition between high school and university can be pretty challenging.

508
00:31:00,000 --> 00:31:04,000
And so AP classes are really going to help prepare students.

509
00:31:04,000 --> 00:31:09,000
And in Richmond as well, so students are studying topics that maybe they're really passionate

510
00:31:09,000 --> 00:31:10,000
about.

511
00:31:10,000 --> 00:31:13,000
They might discover a new career interest or academic pathway they didn't know about

512
00:31:13,000 --> 00:31:14,000
before.

513
00:31:14,000 --> 00:31:17,000
And the research kind of backs all of this up.

514
00:31:17,000 --> 00:31:24,000
If you look at studies done in Canada, students going to UBC or University of Alberta, the

515
00:31:24,000 --> 00:31:29,000
College Board looked at students who took AP courses and compared how they were doing

516
00:31:29,000 --> 00:31:32,000
to those who did not take AP classes.

517
00:31:32,000 --> 00:31:37,000
And the students who took AP classes in high school are doing a lot better in terms of

518
00:31:37,000 --> 00:31:42,000
GPA, their graduate unit higher rates, they are staying in their programs longer.

519
00:31:42,000 --> 00:31:48,000
So yeah, the research backs it up and the universities are aware of this research.

520
00:31:48,000 --> 00:31:52,000
They know that AP classes are going to prepare students and so they're looking for that to

521
00:31:52,000 --> 00:31:56,000
be on students' transcripts.

522
00:31:56,000 --> 00:31:59,000
So yeah, that's kind of speaks to my third point there, which is that it helps you stand

523
00:31:59,000 --> 00:32:02,000
out when you're applying.

524
00:32:02,000 --> 00:32:07,000
It shows universities that you're ready to challenge yourself academically, that you're

525
00:32:07,000 --> 00:32:10,000
too ready to move to the next level.

526
00:32:10,000 --> 00:32:14,000
And then the last reason to take an AP class is it can potentially save you a lot of time

527
00:32:14,000 --> 00:32:18,000
and money once you begin attending university because I mentioned earlier, if you do well

528
00:32:18,000 --> 00:32:23,000
enough on the exam, you can potentially get credit for that course.

529
00:32:23,000 --> 00:32:29,000
And so if students choose to use that credit, they'd be saving a lot of money and also time.

530
00:32:30,000 --> 00:32:34,000
Okay, so here are some questions I get asked a lot about AP.

