768
00:47:05,000 --> 00:47:07,000
It is a required course for graduation.

769
00:47:07,000 --> 00:47:09,000
It's a four credit course.

770
00:47:10,000 --> 00:47:18,000
And then Ms. Manning and I teach the Career Life Connections 11 and 12 courses.

771
00:47:18,000 --> 00:47:22,000
Those courses are taught outside the timetable and they're also required for graduation.

772
00:47:22,000 --> 00:47:26,000
And then we also coordinate the work experience component as well for senior students.

773
00:47:26,000 --> 00:47:28,000
So we'll get into that in the next few slides.

774
00:47:30,000 --> 00:47:36,000
So the Career Life Education, so those courses we were talking about, the grade 10 course, as mentioned, is mandatory for graduation.

775
00:47:36,000 --> 00:47:39,000
Students take that as one of their eight classes that they take.

776
00:47:39,000 --> 00:47:44,000
The CLC 11 and 12, the Career Life Connections 11 and 12 courses, we meet a couple of times during the year.

777
00:47:44,000 --> 00:47:48,000
In fact, we met with all the grade 12s last Friday and we're meeting with all the grade 11s this Friday.

778
00:47:49,000 --> 00:47:53,000
That content is delivered through meetings and assignments through teams.

779
00:47:54,000 --> 00:48:01,000
The culmination of the career courses is the capstone presentation, which students do in April of their grade 12 year.

780
00:48:01,000 --> 00:48:07,000
And that capstone presentation is really just a presentation of their learning journey from grade 10 through to grade 12,

781
00:48:08,000 --> 00:48:13,000
including also what their next steps are after they leave high school.

782
00:48:14,000 --> 00:48:21,000
So really, that's the purpose of the career programs is to get them ready for and make a plan for what are they going to do when they leave here?

783
00:48:21,000 --> 00:48:23,000
What are those next steps look like?

784
00:48:23,000 --> 00:48:30,000
Yeah, our role is to complement what's happening in the classroom here at the school by providing students with opportunities to get involved in the community

785
00:48:30,000 --> 00:48:37,000
and help build their portfolio and get ready for next steps, whether that be going to work or going to post-secondary right after high school.

786
00:48:38,000 --> 00:48:41,000
Part of that is that students need to do some work experience to graduate.

787
00:48:41,000 --> 00:48:43,000
And this is community work experience.

788
00:48:43,000 --> 00:48:46,000
So it could be paid, could be volunteer, a combination of.

789
00:48:47,000 --> 00:48:50,000
Minimum requirement to graduate is 30 hours.

790
00:48:50,000 --> 00:48:57,000
But most of our students here take an elective in grade 12 called Work Experience 12A, which includes 80 hours of work experience.

791
00:48:58,000 --> 00:49:09,000
And then students do that on weekends after school, on breaks, especially like summer break is a big time when students get out because they have lots of time to build and build their resume and work.

792
00:49:10,000 --> 00:49:14,000
There's lots of great reasons why doing work experience is important.

793
00:49:14,000 --> 00:49:17,000
Again, supporting what students are doing in the classroom.

794
00:49:17,000 --> 00:49:25,000
We want to get them out exploring different careers, figure out what they like, what they don't like, help them build some skills, build their resumes

795
00:49:25,000 --> 00:49:31,000
so that when they apply for scholarships or when they go to job interviews, they have experiences they can draw upon.

796
00:49:32,000 --> 00:49:37,000
A lot of our students end up getting part time work, too, from the different experiences that they do in the community,

797
00:49:38,000 --> 00:49:45,000
the networking that they that they build, they they meet mentors, they get advice and connect with adults and other peers in the community.

798
00:49:45,000 --> 00:49:51,000
And that's how they learn about different programs and different opportunities that are available to them.

799
00:49:51,000 --> 00:49:59,000
And then they make references from professional contacts and they'll help them when they apply to university and also when they present their capstone in grade 12.

800
00:50:01,000 --> 00:50:05,000
So if you're wondering what work experience opportunities are available, the students are all in teams.

801
00:50:06,000 --> 00:50:10,000
Work experience is completed in grade 11 and grade 12.

802
00:50:10,000 --> 00:50:14,000
So for the graduation requirement, students do need to be in grade 11 and grade 12.

803
00:50:14,000 --> 00:50:17,000
Students can, of course, be volunteering in grade 8, 9 and 10.

804
00:50:17,000 --> 00:50:23,000
But the program that we have here at the school supports students through their grade 11 and grade 12 year to get involved in the community.

805
00:50:23,000 --> 00:50:27,000
And it's only during those two years that they can complete the 30 hours needed for graduation.

806
00:50:27,000 --> 00:50:30,000
